spec:
  grid: 15-30 rows x 15-30 cols
  background: 0 (most common color)
  frame:
    shape: monochrome rectangle with 1-cell-thick border enclosing a layout of holes (bg cells) and walls (frame-color cells)
    layout: 4-12 rows x 4-8 cols inner grid; holes = 20-50% of layout cells
    slots: 3-6 connected (4-conn) hole regions, each 8-separated from others; areas range 1-7 cells
    includes_unit_slots: 1-2 slots of area 1 per example [observed]
  pieces:
    count: equals number of slots (one piece per slot)
    structure: each piece is a k*k-block-scaled version of its matching slot shape (possibly rotated/flipped under dihedral group)
    k: 2-3 (block scale factor); inferred as side of smallest solid-square piece
    color: each piece is monochrome; non-unit pieces have distinct colors; unit-slot pieces (k*k solid blocks) may share a color
    placement: scattered outside the frame bbox on the bg, separated from frame and each other by >= 1 bg cell
  distractors:
    type: single-pixel noise in a single dedicated color (distinct from frame and all piece colors)
    count: 8-13 singleton pixels scattered across the grid
  output:
    size: (layout_h + 2) * k  x  (layout_w + 2) * k
    content: frame-color background with each piece placed at its matching slot position (scaled by k, with 1-block-width border)
    colors_dropped: frame color becomes bg; distractor color removed entirely

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick k in {2, 3}, frame_color, and layout dimensions (4-12 x 4-8).
    2. Design the layout grid (holes vs walls) ensuring 3-6 slots that are 4-connected internally and 8-separated from each other; include 1-2 unit slots; hole density 20-50%.
    3. For each slot, choose a distinct piece color and apply a random dihedral transform, then upscale the slot mask by k to get the piece sprite (solid k*k blocks). Unit slots become k*k solid squares (may share a color).
    4. Build the output: (layout_h+2)*k x (layout_w+2)*k grid of frame_color, paste each piece at (slot_r+1)*k, (slot_c+1)*k.
    5. Build the input: place the frame (layout bordered by 1 cell of frame_color) anywhere on a bg=0 grid large enough to fit frame + all pieces with spacing. Scatter pieces outside the frame with >= 1 cell bg gap. Add 8-13 singleton distractor pixels in a fresh color.
```
